# About
Added export of SWRConfigContext to allow for
 - consuming context in class components (such as [error boundaries](https://reactjs.org/docs/error-boundaries.html))
 - mocking SWRConfigContext in fixtures/tests

It seems like retrying errors isn't currently possible with suspense (#1907). This change allows clearing/manipulating the cache before resuming from an error boundary.

# Example usage

```tsx
export class ErrorGuard extends Component<any, { error: Error | undefined }> {
  constructor(props: any) {
    super(props);
    this.state = { error: undefined };
  }

  public componentDidCatch(error: any, errorInfo: any) {
    this.setState({ error });
  }

  public render() {
    if (this.state.error === undefined) {
      return <Fragment {...this.props} />;
    }

    return (
      <SWRConfigContext.Consumer>
        {value => 
          <div>
            <div>Error</div>
            <button onClick={() => { value.cache.delete("somekey"); this.setState({ error: undefined }) }}>Retry</button>
          </div>
        }
      </SWRConfigContext.Consumer>
    );
  }
}
```

Additional functionality to automatically refetch errors on mount when using suspense would be a more useful option (can be done in a separate PR)

